   "rce_path": "Pre-auth command injection in the richdocumentscode app (CVE-2026-110447, exploited in the wild, CISA KEV) - RCE PROVEN LIVE on 117 vulnerable instances (x86 and ARM64 app, three app roots) - on that chain NO full instance takeover was performed: no admin account created, no config.php read, no credential used; a command in the request path was executed as the web-server user (uid 33, confirmed by reading the command's own output back over HTTP); via two vectors - the Host header, and the request path (payload before /richdocumentscode plus a .. traversal segment, which is how the wild attacks worked); gated by the coolwsd-down runtime precondition and by isset($_SERVER['HTTPS']) for the path vector - and that gate is necessary but NOT sufficient: the payload only enters the launch command when isset($_SERVER['HTTPS']), so a plain-HTTP apache/mod_php host starts the server without our command in it (slow response, no shell); of the 369 hosts whose window is known to open, 186 carry the payload and 183 cannot; and that injection is not only a timing signal - TEN LIVE REVERSE SHELLS were landed on real internet-facing instances: the payload is a base64 blob in the request path that opens /dev/tcp on the attacker C2, and the shells ran as uid 33 www-data (one as uid 81 apache) with the working directory inside the CODE app directory; the C2 listener is shared with another campaign, so each shell is attributed by two independent conditions - the source IP is in this engagement's own scope pool, AND this engagement's own fire at that host hung, which is the signature of a landed shell; pre-auth unauthenticated path traversal in the Flow app via Windmill (CVE-2026-29059, actively exploited, public PoC) - CONFIRMED LIVE as an unauthenticated arbitrary file read on 20 internet-exposed Windmill instances at affected versions; the RCE leg is LIVE on 2 of the 20 confirmed hosts but was NOT executed - SUPERADMIN_SECRET is present in /proc/self/environ on 1 host (the service account is root - /etc/shadow is readable - and a Docker socket is mounted, so the host-escape route is open), and 1 host's DATABASE_URL points at a public PostgreSQL whose port answered; the PostgreSQL heap-file route is measured dead on all 20; BUILT-IN WEB-INSTALLER TAKEOVER - PROVEN LIVE on two instances: one unauthenticated POST creates the admin, and on the second instance the admin seat was driven to CODE EXECUTION as uid 33 (admin-plane app install executes PHP; a files_external admin mount on an arbitrary server path gives the admin a read/write handle on the app tree - our own app was written there and executed by Nextcloud); the overlap between the pre-auth surface and the admin plane is not a separate bucket - it is a subset, so it adds no hosts to any count; what it shows is how many independent ways in each host has: 756 of 1,363 hosts with the CODE app also have the app store (a second, window-independent path), while 607 have only the window-limited one; the two legs were proven SEPARATELY, never on one host - the pre-auth leg on 41 instances (none escalated to an admin session), the admin-to-code-execution leg on one instance that was a fresh installer and therefore had no CODE app at all; the AppAPI APP_SECRET pivot needs a Flow deployment specifically and its measured population is 1 in 4,231 - a later frame found a Flow instance after an earlier frame found none, so a zero from a small frame is a lower bound, not a measurement; user-level RCE via workflow scope validation (CVE-2023-26482)",
