   "source_notes": "Old hosting. RECENCY-FILTERED (permanent rule, operator 2026-11-19): after=\"2026-09-11\" takes this row's ZoomEye count from 227,612 to 9,817 - the unfiltered number is a count of index records, most of whose hosts no longer exist. population is the ZoomEye title=\"Vesta\" count (227,612), a CONTAINS match on the panel's <title>Vesta - Login</title> - its marker precision was never measured, so the figure is a candidate total, not a population.  Needs a host list and a probe of the marker (one GET per host, read the title and the /images/vesta_logo.png reference).  ZoomEye is currently returning 402 credits_insufficient, so neither the census nor the probe could be run today.  Precise markers for when the credits are back: http.body=\"vesta_logo.png\", title=\"Vesta - Login\", title==\"Vesta - Login\", or http.header.server=\"nginx\" && port=8083. 2026-11-19: the population figure here (227,612) comes from title=\"Vesta\", which is a CONTAINS match on the panel's page title (<title>Vesta - Login</title>) and is NOT verified - urlscan shows the same string matching unrelated sites such as vesta-partners.ch.  It needs a probe before it is used as an exposure figure.  Precise markers, from the source: http.body=\"vesta_logo.png\" (the login page references /images/vesta_logo.png), title=\"Vesta - Login\", or http.header.server=\"nginx\" && port=8083.  The panel listens on 8083 and the stock firewall opens it to 0.0.0.0/0.  ZoomEye is currently returning 402 credits_insufficient, so the census could not be re-run or probed today.  Workspace: /root/VestaCP-RCE-2026t/docs/VESTACP.md",
   "in_unified": true,
   "in_census": true,
   "takeover": "secret",
   "takeover_note": "No first-visit claim window: VestaCP's installer is CLI-only (vst-install.sh) and there is no web installer that lets the first visitor create the admin - both /list/user/ and /add/user/ require an existing admin session.  The admin password instead exists from install time and is printed out of band (install output + mail to the admin address).  TWO INSTALL-WINDOW FACTS, verified in the source 2026-11-19: (1) the installer takes the password on the command line (-p), so an automated install - VPS template, cloud image, provisioning script - can hardcode it, which is permanent mass compromise rather than a window; (2) when -p is absent the password is generated by gen_pass() as 10 characters from [0-9A-Za-z] using bash $RANDOM, i.e. a non-CSPRNG with ~32 bits of real entropy seeded from time+PID, and the interactive installer never asks for a password at all - it prompts only for email, port and FQDN.  There is no forced password change on first login.  Separately there IS an exposure window during the install itself: nginx, php-fpm, vsftpd, exim and dovecot are started (installer lines 1016, 1073, 1104, 1266, 1292) BEFORE the admin account is created (line 1439), so the mail stack is reachable while the host firewall and fail2ban are not yet in place.  The account-takeover route is CVE-2020-10966 instead: the pre-auth password-reset endpoint puts $_SERVER['HTTP_HOST'] in the reset mail, so a Host-header injection captures the reset code - that needs a victim click, not a claim.",
   "noise": false
