   "rce_path": "Nagios is a family; the RCE surface differs per member. UNAUTHENTICATED RCE paths, and what was actually found live: XI 5.2.6-5.4.12 core-config-manager chain (CVE-2018-8733 auth bypass -> CVE-2018-8734 SQLi in selInfoKey1 -> CVE-2018-8735 command injection via backend/index.php -> CVE-2018-8736 root): the three artefacts (settings.php, helpedit.php, backend/index.php) were confirmed present on ONE live instance, and the chain was NOT executed; XI <=5.5.7 RSS dashlet MagpieRSS (CVE-2018-20171/20172/15708): one live instance carries the scripts and honours the url parameter, but the fetch there goes through the PHP curl extension (libcurl errors: 'Invalid protocol', 'connection failed (11)') so the command-injection sink is ABSENT - TESTED, NEGATIVE, no command ran; NagiosQL <=2.00 RFI (CVE-2007-2709/2710) and CCM <=2012R2.4 SQLi (CVE-2013-6875): no instance at those versions - the CCM instances found are 3.2-3.5; Nagios Core statuswml.cgi command injection (CVE-2009-2288), history.cgi (CVE-2012-6096) and cmd.cgi (CVE-2014-1878): no unauthenticated Core instance - both Core instances found put HTTP Basic auth in front of the CGIs; NRPE (CVE-2013-1362, CVE-2014-2913, CVE-2020-6581, CVE-2020-6582): no instance exposes 5666 - the search engines do not scan that port, so this surface is invisible to a body/title index; NDOUtils (CVE-2024-43199), Thruk (CVE-2024-39915). NO LIVE RCE HAS BEEN PROVEN FOR NAGIOS - the unauthenticated surface is historical: the XI 5.x generation carried it, the current generation does not.",
